# What provides each tool in config/.
#
# Read by bin/dotfiles-doctor through bin/lib/util.sh's manifest_rows, and
# checked by bin/dotfiles-lint's `owners` case. This file is data, not a shell
# source: bin/dotfiles-lint globs bin/lib/*.sh, so it is deliberately not linted
# or formatted.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS
#
# install.conf.yaml globs config/* into ~/.config/, so a directory added here is
# live configuration the moment it is committed — whether or not the tool it
# configures is installed by anything in this repository. Four of the entries
# below turned out to have no installer at all, and the only way to find that
# out was to check each one by hand.
#
# So this file is a forcing function rather than a record: `just lint owners`
# fails when config/ holds an entry that is not listed, and when a row names an
# entry that is gone. Adding a config directory therefore requires saying what
# installs its tool, and "nothing does" is a legitimate answer that stays
# visible instead of being rediscovered a year later.
#
# It is NOT a check that the tool is installed *now*. That is per-host and
# changes under you; bin/dotfiles-doctor answers it at runtime, from this file.
#
# FORMAT
#
# One entry per line, four fields separated by a single "|" with NO padding —
# a space next to a "|" becomes part of a field — plus an optional fifth.
# "#" starts a comment.
#
#   entry|kind|provider|note
#   entry|kind|provider|note|hosts
#
#   entry     a name directly under config/, file or directory, verbatim
#             (including any extension: `cship.toml`, not `cship`)
#   kind      brew    a formula or cask in at least one homebrew/<host>
#             mise    a tool in config/mise/mise.toml
#             gh-ext  a GitHub CLI extension in packages/gh-extensions
#             fisher  a fish plugin in config/fish/fish_plugins
#             setup   installed directly by a setup.sh step
#             mason   installed by Neovim's Mason, outside this repository
#             manual  present on a machine, installed by nothing here
#             orphan  nothing provides it, and nothing is expected to
#   provider  the name to look for under that kind — NOT always the entry name.
#             `nvim` is provided by the mise tool `neovim`; `gh-dash` by the gh
#             extension `dlvhdr/gh-dash`.
#   note      free text, or "-"
#   hosts     OPTIONAL. A comma-separated list of hostnames, each of which must
#             name a file in homebrew/. Absent or empty means every host, which
#             is the normal case — only write it when the tool genuinely
#             belongs to particular machines.
#
# ON hosts
#
# The field exists because "macbook-2019 only" used to live in the *note*,
# where doctor printed it and then reported the finding anyway. `borders` and
# `wezterm` are installed on that machine and nowhere else, so on the other two
# `check_packages` asked "is it here", correctly answered no, and told you to
# fix something that was not broken — on every run, forever (SI-125). A check
# that cannot go green stops being read.
#
# A scoped entry is still checked on the hosts it names, and is still printed
# under `--verbose` on the others, so it does not become invisible. Making an
# entry invisible is the failure this file was built to prevent; making it
# quiet where it does not apply is the point.
#
# It is deliberately the LAST field, so the thirty rows that apply everywhere
# stay byte-identical and a diff shows only what actually changed.
#
# ON kind FOR A TOOL THAT HAS TWO PROVIDERS
#
# Thirteen of these are in both a Brewfile and config/mise/mise.toml. The kind
# records the one that is *meant* to win — mise, since SI-118 — and doctor
# reports the overlap as a finding rather than this file pretending it is fine.
# atuin is the clearest case: mise-managed on macbook-m5-pro and a brew formula
# on the other two, which is why packages/services starts it conditionally.

aerospace|brew|nikitabobko/tap/aerospace|cask; window manager
atuin|mise|atuin|also a brew formula on mac-mini and macbook-2019
bat|mise|bat|also brew; bat-extras is mise-only
borders|brew|felixkratz/formulae/borders|started via packages/services|macbook-2019
cship.toml|manual|cship|no installer anywhere; the binary is at ~/.local/bin/cship
doom|setup|doom-emacs|git-cloned by setup.sh's editors step, not packaged
fish|brew|fish|the login shell; setup.sh's packages step must supply it
gh|mise|gh|also brew; see the gh wrapper in docs/environment.md
gh-dash|gh-ext|dlvhdr/gh-dash|a gh extension, not a formula — no Brewfile will name it
ghostty|brew|ghostty|cask; the actual terminal
git|brew|git|arrives as a dependency on some hosts, so it may be absent from the dump
harper-ls|mason|harper-ls|a Neovim LSP installed by Mason; nothing here references it
herdr|mise|herdr|also brew; plugins come from packages/herdr-plugins
hunk|mise|hunk|also brew on mac-mini and macbook-2019; config/git/config sets it as pager
lazydocker|mise|lazydocker|also brew
lazygit|mise|lazygit|also brew
lf|brew|lf|icons come from the lf-icons fisher plugin
mise|brew|mise|mise is installed from brew; it cannot install itself
nushell|brew|nushell|config/nushell/env.nu is generated — see shell/README.md
nvim|mise|neovim|the directory is nvim, the mise tool is neovim
oatmeal|brew|dustinblackman/tap/oatmeal|-
opencode|mise|opencode|also brew, spelled two ways across hosts
ripgrep|mise|ripgrep|also brew
sbx|brew|docker/tap/sbx|cask; the pi and omp kits under config/sbx/kits are this repo's
sesh|brew|joshmedeski/sesh/sesh|-
starship.toml|mise|starship|also brew; the prompt
superfile|mise|superfile|also brew
tmux|brew|tmux|deliberately not mise — config/mise/mise.toml says why
wezterm|brew|wezterm|cask; Ghostty is the terminal elsewhere|macbook-2019
worktrunk|mise|worktrunk|also brew
yazi|mise|yazi|also brew
zed|brew|zed|cask
